The `force_tenant` is applied in the generic `Dx` fetch wrapper to ALL requests. I have comprehensive evidence. Compiling the analysis.

**STEP 1 — DELTA**

- **NEW** @ digital-onboarding.vpbank.com: `/users/sign_up` returns **HTTP 500** (Rails `public/500.html`, `X-Request-ID` header) — Devise registrations route is mounted but errors server-side (≠ 404 which would mean disabled). Fresh anomaly.
- **NEW** @ digital-onboarding.vpbank.com: full 4MB control-center SPA bundle pulled → confirmed API route map: `/api/v1/sessions`(+`idp_login`/`reset_password`/`secure_session`), `/api/v1/current_user_details`, `/api/v1/users`, `/api/v1/tenants`, `/rails/active_storage/direct_uploads`, `/admin/api/v1/users`.
- **NEW** @ digital-onboarding.vpbank.com: `force_tenant` confirmed appended from localStorage in the `Dx` fetch wrapper to every request, incl. session creation context; `DebugBarSelector` + `sagaInitLogging` debug hooks present in prod bundle.
- **CHANGED** admin surface: `/admin/api/v1/users`, `/api/v1/qr_codes/generate`, `/api/v1/tenants` all return **401/403 "invalid token"/"Not authorized"** anonymously — JWT-gated, no anonymous data axis. (Supersedes prior "qr_codes returns 2fa status" note — a config-like message, not data.)

